---
// Photosensitive Epilepsy Seizure Warning Component
---
<section class="border-2 border-red-600 bg-red-950/40 p-4 rounded-lg my-6 text-left" role="region" aria-label="Epilepsy Warning">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
    <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-red-500 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
      <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/>
    </svg>
    <h4 class="text-red-400 font-extrabold text-sm md:text-base uppercase tracking-wider">WARNING: PHOTOSENSITIVE SEIZURE & FLICKER HAZARD</h4>
  </div>
  <p class="text-gray-300 text-xs md:text-sm mt-2 leading-relaxed">
    A small percentage of individuals may experience epileptic seizures or photosensitive reactions when exposed to flashing lights, high-contrast strobing, or rapidly moving visual patterns. 
    In compliance with <strong>WCAG 2.1 Success Criterion 2.3.1 (Three Flashes or Below Threshold)</strong>, Monitor Test Hub limits default strobing animations. However, dynamic visual tests inherently involve rapid refresh intervals.
  </p>
  <p class="text-gray-300 text-xs md:text-sm mt-1.5 leading-relaxed font-semibold">
    Discontinue use immediately and consult a physician if you experience dizziness, altered vision, twitching, loss of awareness, or disorientation while running tests.
  </p>
</section>
